pr_body:
Closes: #106 

This PR fixes an issue with babel transpiled import for fs.readFileSync:
```js
var _fs = require("fs");

var _fs2 = _interopRequireDefault(_fs);

function _interopRequireDefault(obj) { return obj && obj.__esModule ? obj : { default: obj }; }

var name = _fs2.default.readFileSync(__driname + '/name.text');
document.body.innerHTML = "Hello, " + name + "! Inlining via fs.readFileSync is working!";
```

It sort of simplifies `referencesImport` method, but at the same time it's not the "most performant" solution (traverse couple of times) :( I ran tests several times and couldn't see any performance regressions, but they are too small to be able to reveal any perf impact.

Also i re-enabled fs-import test. It wasn't included for, i guess, the same reason.

Another option could be detecting babel presets/plugins that transpile imports and show error message.
